  \"model_expression\": \"P(Finland wins) = P(Qualifies) × P(Song Quality > 85th percentile) × f(Nordic bloc, Public advantage, Competitive field) where f() represents complex interaction of voting dynamics. Approximate: 0.85 × 0.15 × (0.75 × 0.3 / 6 competitors) ≈ 0.024 or 2.4%\",
  \"confidence\": 0.72,
  \"reasoning\": \"High confidence in historical data (Eurovision results are well-documented). Medium confidence in voting pattern analysis (patterns are stable but evolving). Low confidence in 2026-specific factors (song quality unknown, competitive field unknown, 18 months of potential geopolitical/cultural shifts). The 2023 near-win provides recent evidence of Finland's competitive potential, but also shows how close margins are and how jury-public splits affect outcomes. Base rate of 1.5% is likely conservative given Finland's recent momentum, but 2026 is far enough out that regression to mean is expected. Overall confidence of 0.72 reflects strong historical foundation but significant uncertainty about future-specific variables.\"
}
```"
    relevance: 0.5p
    date: 2026-03-05
